{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semantic change in narrative semantic change in narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md","fileName":"Semantic Change in Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semantic Change in Narrative","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 10:07\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semantic change in narrative semantic change in narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Change in Narrative.md","fileName":"Semantic Change in Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semantic Change in Narrative","heading":"Semantic Change in Narrative","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The book uses two complementary views of narrative semantics. A Euclidean factor map expresses the web of relationships among scenes and words; a hierarchy over their sequence can mark novelty, anomaly, or a major turn in that web.\n\nIn its Casablanca example, adjacent scenes that merge only high in the sequence-constrained tree signal stronger change than scenes joined low down. The same principle applies to sub-scenes or tweets. A breakpoint is an analytical indication for interpretation, not proof that one unique human reading is correct.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"propertie